! WHICH VFL AND CONNECTIVE OPERATIONS DATA FETCH (DF) APPLIES TO, AND
! WHETHER A SUPPRESSED ONE FETCHES -- one classification, asked by both
! StretchIBox.prepareExec and execute() (StretchExecute vflRef,
! connFetchType, fieldDfSuppresses), 2026-11-18.
!
! THE RULE.  Reference Manual 22-6530-2 printed p.32 (PDF 35), page image:
! "When an address alarm is caused by a data address used in a fetch-type
! operation, indicator DF is turned on.  If the DF mask bit is one, the
! data fetch is suppressed and the operation terminated.  If the DF mask
! bit is zero, the operation proceeds normally.  A fetch-type operation is
! one in which the contents of an addressed storage location are read out
! for use but are not subject to change by the operation."  And DS: "A
! store-type operation is one in which the contents of an addressed
! storage location are subject to change."  Printed p.45 item 20 (PDF 48):
! "If the corresponding mask bit was one, the fetch did not take place,
! and the entire operation was suppressed.  If the mask bit was zero, the
! operation was completed normally."  So +MG (printed p.60), KF, KE, KFE,
! KR, KFR (pp.65-67), * (p.68), / (p.70), LCV and LTRCV (pp.72-73) are
! fetch-type; ST, SRD, M+, M+MG, M+1 and CM are store-type (DS, never
! DF); CV and DCV (pp.73-74) take their field from the accumulator and
! address no storage.  StretchExecute's vflRef note quotes each page.
!
! THE BUG.  execute() signalled and suppressed DF for seven codes only (L,
! LWF, +, K, LFT, LTRS, *+), prepareExec for every non-immediate code and
! the first word only.  So a protected * with DF's mask one was loaded with
! no operand address, and the E-box read the protected word itself,
! multiplied by it and never set DF.  MEASURED on 9eb7d27 plus the read
! counter (before the fix) with this deck: resae = (16)7C7C2000..., resdf =
! (16)00301000..., resds = (16)000C2000... -- DF's routine ran for cases 10 and 11 only, and the mask-zero * and +MG (16,
! 17) did not set DF; the protected operation changed the accumulator in
! cases 0 and 6-8.  (That run had 20 cases; 20 and 21 were added after.)
!
! SHAPE.  The setup is cwf_data_fetch_suppress's (boundaries WLOW..WABOVE,
! control bit 0: signal inside; DF's routine sets word 6 bit 1, DS's
! word 6 bit 0).  Each case reloads the accumulator with PAT2W, runs six
! I-box-only LVIs, the case's operation, a K against PAT2W and eight NOPs,
! and records three bits: RESAE.k (AE after that K: the accumulator is
! unchanged), RESDF.k (DF's routine ran at mask one; the DF indicator is on
! at mask zero) and RESDS.k (DS's routine ran).
!   0-9   +MG KF KE KFE KR KFR * / LCV LTRCV on WHIGH, mask one: suppressed
!   10    L across UNPROT|WLOW, mask one: DF on the SECOND word suppresses
!   11    CT on WHIGH, mask one (connective, already DF'd)
!   12-13 ST, CM on WHIGH, mask one: DS, not DF
!   14-15 CV, DCV naming WHIGH: no storage operand, nothing
!   16-19 *, +MG, ST, crossing L at mask ZERO: DF on and the operation
!         completes; ST is DS's as at mask one
!   20-21 ST, CM behind an unprotected divide, mask one: the store's level
!         waits in the look-ahead, so whether it fetched shows in CYCLES
! EXPECTED and observed: resae = (16)FFFC2000..., resdf = (16)FFF0D000...,
! resds = (16)000C2C00....
!
! THE READ COUNT.  MEMREADS (tests/gen_tb.py) is the number of storage
! reads the run made (StretchMemory MBCU.readCount).  It pins whether a
! level fetched at all, which no CYCLES pin could see for the VFL and
! connective DF clauses (cwf_data_fetch_suppress's header).
!
! INJECTIONS, each in a scratch copy of the tree, the file restored from a
! saved copy and compared with cmp against the worktree (IDENTICAL every
! time), both this deck and cwf_data_fetch_suppress run -- OBSERVED:
!   CONTROL                                  -> both decks green
!   I1 * classed store-type (execute and     -> resae (16)FDFC2..., resdf
!      prepareExec both skip DF for it)         (16)FDF05... (cases 6, 16),
!                                               CYCLES 5974, MEMREADS 563
!   I2 prepareExec's VflInt DF clause gone   -> CYCLES 6049, MEMREADS 580;
!                                               cwf_data_fetch_suppress
!                                               MEMREADS 63 (CYCLES 824 kept)
!   I3 prepareExec's Connective DF clause    -> MEMREADS 570 only;
!      gone                                     cwf_data_fetch_suppress
!                                               MEMREADS 63 only
!   I4 prepareExec's VflInt clause back to   -> CYCLES 6040, MEMREADS 570
!      the old one (every code, word 1)
!   I5 prepareExec's Connective clause back  -> CYCLES 6040 only (case 21)
!      to the old one (CM included)
!   I6 fieldDfSuppresses asks word 1 only    -> resae (16)FFDC2... (case 10
!                                               not suppressed), CYCLES
!                                               6036, MEMREADS 570
!   I7 fetchesOperand counts DCV again       -> MEMREADS 570 only
!   I8 CM classed fetch-type                 -> resdf (16)FFF4D4..., resds
!                                               (16)00082800... (cases 13,
!                                               21: DF in place of DS),
!                                               CYCLES 6036, MEMREADS 567
!   I9 prepareExec monitors VFL stores for   -> CYCLES 6040 only (case 20)
!      DF again, nothing else changed
! Every other check passes under each.
!
! CYCLES 6031 AND MEMREADS 569 ARE MODEL BEHAVIOUR; no documented time or
! request count exists for a no-op'd level (Perf. Char. Vol. 1 printed
! A-8, PDF 67, gives only its NOOP tag).  Whether a PROTECTED VFL store
! fetches is not printed either (Perf. Char. Vol. 1 printed p.2-3 item 6:
! "All VFL stores are fetch-and-stores"); the model's does, CHOSEN.
        SLC, (8)4100.0
START   BD,  $+.32                   ! disable while words 3 and 12 are set
        LVI, $X13, TBL
        SV,  $X13, $IA
        LVI, $X13, WLOW
        SV,  $X13, $LB               ! lower boundary := WLOW
        LVI, $X13, WABOVE
        SV,  $X13, $UB               ! upper boundary := WABOVE
        BBZ, 3.57, $+1.0             ! control bit := 0: signal INSIDE
        BBZ, $DF,  $+1.0
        BB1, 12.20, $+1.0            ! DF's mask bit := ONE
        BE,  $+.32                   ! ENABLE
!
! case 0: +MG    fetch-type, newly DF'd
        L(BU,64,8), PAT2W            ! accumulator := PAT2W
        LVI, $X2, 1
        LVI, $X2, 2
        LVI, $X2, 3
        LVI, $X2, 4
        LVI, $X2, 5
        LVI, $X2, 6
        +MG(BU,64,8), WHIGH          ! case 0
        K(BU,64,8), PAT2W            ! E-box work right behind it
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        BZB, $AE,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESAE+.0, $+1.0        ! accumulator unchanged
        BZB, 6.1,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESDF+.0, $+1.0        ! DF's routine ran
        BBZ, 6.1,  $+1.0
        BZB, 6.0,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESDS+.0, $+1.0        ! DS's routine ran
        BBZ, 6.0,  $+1.0
!
! case 1: KF     fetch-type, newly DF'd
        L(BU,64,8), PAT2W            ! accumulator := PAT2W
        LVI, $X2, 1
        LVI, $X2, 2
        LVI, $X2, 3
        LVI, $X2, 4
        LVI, $X2, 5
        LVI, $X2, 6
        KF(BU,64,8), WHIGH           ! case 1
        K(BU,64,8), PAT2W            ! E-box work right behind it
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        BZB, $AE,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESAE+.1, $+1.0        ! accumulator unchanged
        BZB, 6.1,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESDF+.1, $+1.0        ! DF's routine ran
        BBZ, 6.1,  $+1.0
        BZB, 6.0,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESDS+.1, $+1.0        ! DS's routine ran
        BBZ, 6.0,  $+1.0
!
! case 2: KE     fetch-type, newly DF'd (AE on: it compares)
        L(BU,64,8), PAT2W            ! accumulator := PAT2W
        LVI, $X2, 1
        LVI, $X2, 2
        LVI, $X2, 3
        LVI, $X2, 4
        LVI, $X2, 5
        LVI, $X2, 6
        KE(BU,64,8), WHIGH           ! case 2
        K(BU,64,8), PAT2W            ! E-box work right behind it
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        BZB, $AE,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESAE+.2, $+1.0        ! accumulator unchanged
        BZB, 6.1,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESDF+.2, $+1.0        ! DF's routine ran
        BBZ, 6.1,  $+1.0
        BZB, 6.0,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESDS+.2, $+1.0        ! DS's routine ran
        BBZ, 6.0,  $+1.0
!
! case 3: KFE    fetch-type, newly DF'd (AE on: it compares)
        L(BU,64,8), PAT2W            ! accumulator := PAT2W
        LVI, $X2, 1
        LVI, $X2, 2
        LVI, $X2, 3
        LVI, $X2, 4
        LVI, $X2, 5
        LVI, $X2, 6
        KFE(BU,64,8), WHIGH          ! case 3
        K(BU,64,8), PAT2W            ! E-box work right behind it
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        BZB, $AE,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESAE+.3, $+1.0        ! accumulator unchanged
        BZB, 6.1,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESDF+.3, $+1.0        ! DF's routine ran
        BBZ, 6.1,  $+1.0
        BZB, 6.0,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESDS+.3, $+1.0        ! DS's routine ran
        BBZ, 6.0,  $+1.0
!
! case 4: KR     fetch-type, newly DF'd
        L(BU,64,8), PAT2W            ! accumulator := PAT2W
        LVI, $X2, 1
        LVI, $X2, 2
        LVI, $X2, 3
        LVI, $X2, 4
        LVI, $X2, 5
        LVI, $X2, 6
        KR(BU,64,8), WHIGH           ! case 4
        K(BU,64,8), PAT2W            ! E-box work right behind it
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        BZB, $AE,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESAE+.4, $+1.0        ! accumulator unchanged
        BZB, 6.1,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESDF+.4, $+1.0        ! DF's routine ran
        BBZ, 6.1,  $+1.0
        BZB, 6.0,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESDS+.4, $+1.0        ! DS's routine ran
        BBZ, 6.0,  $+1.0
!
! case 5: KFR    fetch-type, newly DF'd
        L(BU,64,8), PAT2W            ! accumulator := PAT2W
        LVI, $X2, 1
        LVI, $X2, 2
        LVI, $X2, 3
        LVI, $X2, 4
        LVI, $X2, 5
        LVI, $X2, 6
        KFR(BU,64,8), WHIGH          ! case 5
        K(BU,64,8), PAT2W            ! E-box work right behind it
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        BZB, $AE,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESAE+.5, $+1.0        ! accumulator unchanged
        BZB, 6.1,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESDF+.5, $+1.0        ! DF's routine ran
        BBZ, 6.1,  $+1.0
        BZB, 6.0,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESDS+.5, $+1.0        ! DS's routine ran
        BBZ, 6.0,  $+1.0
!
! case 6: *      fetch-type, newly DF'd
        L(BU,64,8), PAT2W            ! accumulator := PAT2W
        LVI, $X2, 1
        LVI, $X2, 2
        LVI, $X2, 3
        LVI, $X2, 4
        LVI, $X2, 5
        LVI, $X2, 6
        *(BU,48,8), WHIGH            ! case 6
        K(BU,64,8), PAT2W            ! E-box work right behind it
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        BZB, $AE,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESAE+.6, $+1.0        ! accumulator unchanged
        BZB, 6.1,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESDF+.6, $+1.0        ! DF's routine ran
        BBZ, 6.1,  $+1.0
        BZB, 6.0,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESDS+.6, $+1.0        ! DS's routine ran
        BBZ, 6.0,  $+1.0
!
! case 7: /      fetch-type, newly DF'd
        L(BU,64,8), PAT2W            ! accumulator := PAT2W
        LVI, $X2, 1
        LVI, $X2, 2
        LVI, $X2, 3
        LVI, $X2, 4
        LVI, $X2, 5
        LVI, $X2, 6
        /(BU,48,8), WHIGH            ! case 7
        K(BU,64,8), PAT2W            ! E-box work right behind it
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        BZB, $AE,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESAE+.7, $+1.0        ! accumulator unchanged
        BZB, 6.1,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESDF+.7, $+1.0        ! DF's routine ran
        BBZ, 6.1,  $+1.0
        BZB, 6.0,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESDS+.7, $+1.0        ! DS's routine ran
        BBZ, 6.0,  $+1.0
!
! case 8: LCV    fetch-type, newly DF'd
        L(BU,64,8), PAT2W            ! accumulator := PAT2W
        LVI, $X2, 1
        LVI, $X2, 2
        LVI, $X2, 3
        LVI, $X2, 4
        LVI, $X2, 5
        LVI, $X2, 6
        LCV(BU,48,8), WHIGH, 64      ! case 8
        K(BU,64,8), PAT2W            ! E-box work right behind it
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        BZB, $AE,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESAE+.8, $+1.0        ! accumulator unchanged
        BZB, 6.1,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESDF+.8, $+1.0        ! DF's routine ran
        BBZ, 6.1,  $+1.0
        BZB, 6.0,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESDS+.8, $+1.0        ! DS's routine ran
        BBZ, 6.0,  $+1.0
!
! case 9: LTRCV  fetch-type, newly DF'd
        L(BU,64,8), PAT2W            ! accumulator := PAT2W
        LVI, $X2, 1
        LVI, $X2, 2
        LVI, $X2, 3
        LVI, $X2, 4
        LVI, $X2, 5
        LVI, $X2, 6
        LTRCV(BU,48,8), WHIGH        ! case 9
        K(BU,64,8), PAT2W            ! E-box work right behind it
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        BZB, $AE,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESAE+.9, $+1.0        ! accumulator unchanged
        BZB, 6.1,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESDF+.9, $+1.0        ! DF's routine ran
        BBZ, 6.1,  $+1.0
        BZB, 6.0,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESDS+.9, $+1.0        ! DS's routine ran
        BBZ, 6.0,  $+1.0
!
! case 10: L      field CROSSING into WLOW: DF on word 2
        L(BU,64,8), PAT2W            ! accumulator := PAT2W
        LVI, $X2, 1
        LVI, $X2, 2
        LVI, $X2, 3
        LVI, $X2, 4
        LVI, $X2, 5
        LVI, $X2, 6
        L(BU,32,8), UNPROT+.48       ! case 10
        K(BU,64,8), PAT2W            ! E-box work right behind it
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        BZB, $AE,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESAE+.10, $+1.0        ! accumulator unchanged
        BZB, 6.1,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESDF+.10, $+1.0        ! DF's routine ran
        BBZ, 6.1,  $+1.0
        BZB, 6.0,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESDS+.10, $+1.0        ! DS's routine ran
        BBZ, 6.0,  $+1.0
!
! case 11: CT     connective fetch-type (already DF'd)
        L(BU,64,8), PAT2W            ! accumulator := PAT2W
        LVI, $X2, 1
        LVI, $X2, 2
        LVI, $X2, 3
        LVI, $X2, 4
        LVI, $X2, 5
        LVI, $X2, 6
        CT0011(BU,64,8), WHIGH       ! case 11
        K(BU,64,8), PAT2W            ! E-box work right behind it
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        BZB, $AE,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESAE+.11, $+1.0        ! accumulator unchanged
        BZB, 6.1,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESDF+.11, $+1.0        ! DF's routine ran
        BBZ, 6.1,  $+1.0
        BZB, 6.0,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESDS+.11, $+1.0        ! DS's routine ran
        BBZ, 6.0,  $+1.0
!
! case 12: ST     STORE-type: DS, never DF
        L(BU,64,8), PAT2W            ! accumulator := PAT2W
        LVI, $X2, 1
        LVI, $X2, 2
        LVI, $X2, 3
        LVI, $X2, 4
        LVI, $X2, 5
        LVI, $X2, 6
        ST(BU,64,8), WHIGH           ! case 12
        K(BU,64,8), PAT2W            ! E-box work right behind it
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        BZB, $AE,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESAE+.12, $+1.0        ! accumulator unchanged
        BZB, 6.1,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESDF+.12, $+1.0        ! DF's routine ran
        BBZ, 6.1,  $+1.0
        BZB, 6.0,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESDS+.12, $+1.0        ! DS's routine ran
        BBZ, 6.0,  $+1.0
!
! case 13: CM     STORE-type: DS, never DF
        L(BU,64,8), PAT2W            ! accumulator := PAT2W
        LVI, $X2, 1
        LVI, $X2, 2
        LVI, $X2, 3
        LVI, $X2, 4
        LVI, $X2, 5
        LVI, $X2, 6
        CM0011(BU,64,8), WHIGH       ! case 13
